        "text": "Design-build means one company handles both the design and construction of your project. Rather than hiring a separate architect or interior designer who then hands off to a contractor, B&B manages everything in-house. The result: tighter communication, faster timelines, clear accountability, and a final product where design intent and execution are perfectly aligned."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long does a bathroom renovation take?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Most bathroom renovations take 3–6 weeks depending on scope, material lead times, and permit requirements. A powder room refresh may complete in 2 weeks, while a full master bath transformation with custom tile work typically runs 5–7 weeks. We provide a detailed project timeline before work begins and update you throughout the process."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you handle permits and inspections?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes — completely. B&B manages all permit applications, municipal inspections, and code compliance across every township we serve in Montgomery County, Bucks County, and the Main Line. You never have to worry about paperwork or inspections. We handle it all as part of the project."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What areas do you serve?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "B&B Associates Creations serves Montgomery County (our primary area — headquartered in Maple Glen), Bucks County, and the Philadelphia Main Line. Our primary towns include Ambler, Blue Bell, North Wales, Lower Gwynedd, Newtown, Doylestown, New Hope, Wayne, Villanova, Bryn Mawr, and Gladwyne. Contact us to confirm service in your area."
      }
    }
  ]
}

